   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Nice. I&#39;ll give that a try and see what happens.<div><br></div><div>The model is on a public URL, it&#39;s available as a permanent link for use anywhere.</div><div><br></div><div>An interesting note if one intends to use shiny with simmer, they don&#39;t play well together. One needs an adapter layer that simply copies all the values over into another object of inputs to feed to simmer. Then shiny sees all the values as used. Shiny does some deep inspection of values and how they are used later to detect when to fire events. simmer when using variables does something that shiny doesn&#39;t see and core events don&#39;t fire. </div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Jun 1, 2017 at 11:55 AM, Iñaki Úcar <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">i.uc...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
